      <tei:div corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:rosh_hashanah/shacharit/repetition/avot/open" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-rishon-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-one-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n124.jpg">
        <tei:p><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-rishon-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-one-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n124.jpg" n="48"/><tei:milestone unit="prayer-part" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:rosh_hashanah/shacharit/repetition/avot/open/text"/><tei:seg source="urn:x-opensiddur:text:prayer:amidah/avot/barukh_attah">Blessed art Thou, O Lord our God and God of our fathers, God of Abraham, God of Isaac and God of Jacob, great, mighty and awe-inspiring God, God the Most High, who performs acts of kindness and owns everything and remembers the good deeds of the fathers and will bring a redeemer for their children’s children for His Name’s sake in love.</tei:seg> <tei:milestone unit="prayer-part"/></tei:p>
